{"type": "standard", "title": "Alagalla Mountain Range", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Alagalla Mountain Range</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "wikibase_item": "Q18209159", "titles": {"canonical": "Alagalla_Mountain_Range", "normalized": "Alagalla Mountain Range", "display": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Alagalla Mountain Range</span></span>"}, "pageid": 43859740, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/A_view_from_Alagalla_Mountain_Range.jpg/330px-A_view_from_Alagalla_Mountain_Range.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 330, "height": 248}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/A_view_from_Alagalla_Mountain_Range.jpg/3840px-A_view_from_Alagalla_Mountain_Range.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 4608, "height": 3456}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "revision": "1368580753", "tid": "cbea9c35-9445-11f1-a227-81c473435b1c", "timestamp": "2026-08-09T22:58:12Z", "description": "Mountain range in Sri Lanka", "description_source": "local", "coordinates": {"lat": 7.25333333, "lon": 80.44638889}, "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alagalla_Mountain_Range", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alagalla_Mountain_Range?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alagalla_Mountain_Range?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Alagalla_Mountain_Range"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alagalla_Mountain_Range", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Alagalla_Mountain_Range", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alagalla_Mountain_Range?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Alagalla_Mountain_Range"}}, "extract": "Alagalla Mountain Range is situated at the boundaries of the Central and Sabaragamuwa Provinces in Sri Lanka. Along with the surrounding Bathalegala (\u0db6\u0dad\u0dbd\u0dda\u0d9c\u0dbd) also known as Bible Rock, Uthuwankanda (\u0d8b\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0d9a\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf), Devanagala (\u0daf\u0dd9\u0dc0\u0db1\u0d9c\u0dbd), Ambuluwawa (\u0d85\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dd4\u0dc5\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dc0), Knuckles Mountain Range and Hanthana (\u0dc4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dcf\u0db1) Mountain Range, Alagalla mountain has served as a natural defense location for nearly five centuries (1505\u20131948) against the Portuguese, Dutch and English invasions aimed at the Kandyan Kingdom.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Alagalla</b> <b>Mountain Range</b> is situated at the boundaries of the Central and Sabaragamuwa Provinces in Sri Lanka. Along with the surrounding <span><span style=\"font-style:normal\">Bathalegala</span></span> (\u0db6\u0dad\u0dbd\u0dda\u0d9c\u0dbd) also known as Bible Rock, <span><span style=\"font-style:normal\">Uthuwankanda</span></span> (\u0d8b\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0d9a\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf), <span><span style=\"font-style:normal\">Devanagala</span></span> (\u0daf\u0dd9\u0dc0\u0db1\u0d9c\u0dbd), <span><span style=\"font-style:normal\">Ambuluwawa</span></span> (\u0d85\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dd4\u0dc5\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dc0), Knuckles Mountain Range and Hanthana (\u0dc4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dcf\u0db1) Mountain Range, Alagalla mountain has served as a natural defense location for nearly five centuries (1505\u20131948) against the Portuguese, Dutch and English invasions aimed at the Kandyan Kingdom.</p>"}